CSR vsetvl VLMAX and PLIC claim arbitration timing fixes (branch timing-fixes, 2026-10-16)
=========================================================================================

Base: fork main 910c023 (L1 caches, PR #15). Host load ~75-130 on 48 cores,
so wall times are pessimistic.

== Per-block synthesis (scripts/synth_block_orfs.sh) ==
ORFS Yosys flow of the full-SoC run (slang, ORFS abc script), Nangate45
typical, OpenSTA on the unrepaired netlist with the liberty wire-load model,
10 ns clock, zero I/O delays. "before" = `git archive origin/main rtl`
(2789d95; muserisc_csr.sv / muserisc_plic.sv are unchanged by 910c023).

block          rev     area (um^2)  worst path                                           delay
muserisc_csr   before  74,032.1     vset_vtype_i[5] -> vl_o[36] (in->reg)                43.148 ns
                                    vset_vtype_i -> vset_vl_o[36] (in->out)              43.108 ns
               after   56,319.9     addr_i[1] -> pmpaddr_q[260] (in->reg)                 0.911 ns
                                    (vsetvl: vset_vl_o no longer in the top paths;
                                     worst in->out pmp_allow_b_o 1.001 ns)
muserisc_plic  before  37,288.1     threshold_q[28] -> claimed_q[16] (reg->reg)          19.195 ns
                                    irq_sources_i[1] -> claimed_q[16] (in->reg)          18.714 ns
                                    -> rdata_o[34] (reg->out)                            19.081 ns
               after   32,859.5     threshold_q[27] -> claimed_q[16] (reg->reg)           3.323 ns
                                    irq_sources_i[23] -> claimed_q[16] (in->reg)          2.772 ns
                                    -> rdata_o[33] (reg->out)                             3.176 ns
Wall: csr 369 s / 99 s, plic 81 s / 56 s.

The block flow reproduces the SoC report (docs/SOC_AREA.md on
soc-sram-synth): CSR 40.3 ns / 73,742 um^2 there, PLIC ~21.4 ns there
(that path also includes the external IRQ input timing and the fabric).
The sv2v + Yosys `synth` flow of scripts/synth_fpu.sh does NOT show the
divider (4.45 ns before): its ABC collapses the 6-input VLMAX function.

== Equivalence ==
- CSR: x / (8 << vsew) for x a power of two = x >> (vsew + 3) for every
  vtype[5:0] (64 combinations, reserved LMUL 4 still 0 -> vill).
- PLIC: lock-step random simulation of the old and new RTL (Verilator,
  4,000,000 cycles; random priorities 0..3 / 0..7 / full 32-bit / all-ones,
  so many ties; random enables, thresholds 0..5, claims and completes):
  rdata_o, eip_o and claimed_q identical every cycle; 200,254 claim reads,
  180,620 of them returning a source.

